    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes: **55 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customerCode de-duplication in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.\n\n**The change:** When a new owner is created, the computed `customerCode` (`<REGION>-<HASH8>`) is now passed through a new `deduplicateCustomerCode` helper before being assigned:\n\n- It collects all existing owners' `customerCode` values into a set.\n- If the base code isn't already in use, it's returned unchanged \u2014 so the normal single-owner case still produces the plain `<REGION>-<HASH8>` code (satisfying Cp09).\n- On a collision, it appends `-<n>`, incrementing `n` from 2 upward until it finds a value not already in use, and returns that de-duplicated code. Each candidate suffix is also checked against the in-use set, so `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 are skipped if they too are taken.\n\nThis guarantees distinct owners always receive distinct customerCodes (satisfying Cp41) while matching the spec's \"smallest n of 2 or more\" rule.",
